yalty programs. The company distributes its products through direct channels, such as the Company's website and the Company's mobile app; and traditional travel agencies, online travel agencies, and other intermediaries. The company was formerly known as United Continental Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to United Airlines Holdings, Inc. in June 2019. United Airlines Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 1968 and is based in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. J. Scott Kirby | CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $9.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 117K people. Revenue per employee of $501K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $22K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 19\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["United Airlines Holdings, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $36.6B market cap on $59.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $2.6B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.51\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.4\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.7%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has 